 ## Supported host and next deployment gate
 
-Support is one Unix host with reliable local filesystem locks, SQLite and the pinned Python runtime. Windows, shared/network filesystems and multiple application hosts are unsupported. PDF admission is bounded to 50 pages/50 MiB, with separate renderer, archive and provider limits. Current live policy uses a one-hour run deadline, 100 provider attempts across the document retry chain, and a per-document cap no greater than $15 within the original shared allowance.
+Support is one Unix host with reliable local filesystem locks, SQLite and the pinned Python runtime. Windows, shared/network filesystems and multiple application hosts are unsupported. PDF admission is bounded to 50 pages/50 MiB, with separate renderer, archive and provider limits. Current live policy uses a one-hour run deadline, 100 provider attempts across the document retry chain, and a per-document cap no greater than $30 within the authorized shared allowance.
 
-Public deployment requires a separate reviewed design and authorization for TLS termination, an explicit trusted-proxy/address boundary, canonical public origin and secure cookies, private durable storage/locking, process supervision, graceful shutdown and retention monitoring. Changing the bind address or inserting a proxy is insufficient. Repeat authentication, ownership, Host/Origin, cancellation, restart and upload-to-download acceptance on the actual deployed URL before calling it a hosted submission.
